{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/cor-gauge-coupling-uniqueness","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Corollary","doco:Section"],"label":"cor:gauge-coupling-uniqueness","kind":"corollary","title":"Uniqueness of the scalar gauge coupling on $A \\otimes A$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-em-spectral-completeness"],"tags":["uniqueness","gauge-coupling","singlet","central-idempotent","no-other-alpha"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.gauge_coupling_uniqueness","text":"gauge-coupling-uniqueness.md","leanSource":"gauge-coupling-uniqueness.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"cor:gauge-coupling-uniqueness\"></a>\n<strong>Corollary.</strong> <em>Uniqueness of the scalar gauge coupling on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A \\otimes A</code></em></p>\n<p><em>Any <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-linear, braid-invariant, scalar coupling <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A \\otimes A \\to \\mathbf{1}</code> is a multiple of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{tr}_\\tau(e_-) \\cdot e_-</code>. Up to the global normalisation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda \\in R</code>, exactly one non-trivial scalar coupling exists on the two-strand sector of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}</code>.</em></p>\n"}
